            <ArticleTitle>Spinal cord compression following labor and delivery with epidural analgesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>256-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Transient back pain is not uncommon during pregnancy and the postpartum period. Following an epidural anesthetic, back pain persisted in a postpartum patient beyond the expected period of soreness. Further diagnostic evaluation led to diagnosis and surgical decompression of a herniated thoracic disc.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
